List options set with environment variables or as a single value in a YAML config (e.g. ``PEAT_HEAT_EXCLUDE_IPS=192.0.2.1,192.0.2.2`` or ``hash_algorithms: md5``) were split into single characters, and a single number (e.g. ``protocol_filter: 502``) failed to load. Strings are now split on commas, or parsed as a JSON or YAML list if they start with ``[``, and a single number becomes a list with one item.
